Chamfers: an analytic chamfer whose contacts both leave their faces before
its edge's ends, into faces beyond that do not reach the ends, cut across
its whole width there by a chain of those faces grown on (mitcad#235).

The case: a thread's groove in a bore ending in a flat face, the edge
where that face meets the bore chamfered further than the groove is deep.
The contact on the flat face lies above the groove's flanks except near
its tip and leaves the face across the tip's edge into the tip's rounding
and on into a flank; the contact on the bore leaves the bore, at one end,
where the next turn of the groove begins. The flanks and the tip, grown on
past the flat face (their surfaces run on along the thread), cut the
chamfer across its whole width at both ends; at one end the cut meets the
contact on the bore past the edge's end, on the prolongation of the
groove's crest edge. Before, SplitKPart left one short piece where both
contacts lie on their faces, and the corners at both ends failed
("OneCorner : bouchon non ecrit").

- ChFi3d_KPartCutChainToEnd (after ChFi3d_KPartCutToEnd and
  ChFi3d_KPartCutToEndOverGap at each end of an open spine of a chamfer
  that takes material off): from where the piece nearest the end has its
  contact on face N leave N on an edge into a face B0, its other side
  ends at that section (SplitKPart left it where that side's own domain
  started), the cut runs over a chain of faces, each crossing an edge
  between two of them (ChFi3d_KPartEdgeCrossing, now also past the edge's
  vertex on N along the isoline of a face's surface the edge runs on,
  ChFi3d_ProlongEdgeAlongIso), up to the face Bn whose surface meets the
  other contact's line at Q, where the blend ends in a point. Q lies on an
  edge Eq of the other contact's face Fo: inside Eq, or on Eq's
  prolongation past the spine's end vertex V along a line, a circle or an
  isoline of its face beyond (ChFi3d_IsolineOfEdge). The pieces are made
  by ChFi3d_KPartChainPieces, on the surface of the piece before them (one
  face). Eq is prolonged to Q bounding Fo and Bn, or, where Q lies inside
  Eq and Eq's face beyond is not Bn, Eq's part from V to Q is replaced by
  a curve bounding that face and Bn (Bn grows up to it). Bn's edges with
  N at V, and the spine's edge at V, lie under the chamfer and bound no
  face any more; the spine's end is a free boundary.
- ChFi3d_KPartCutPiece keeps a given end at a vertex of its own, and
  ChFi3d_MakeExtremities and ChFi3d_FilDS take a blend's end in a point at
  a vertex that is no vertex of the spine as an end in a point that is no
  vertex (before, they looked for that vertex on the spine and threw).
- ChFi3d_Builder::PerformSetOfSurf: a stripe both of whose ends are such
  points of analytic pieces is not computed again as a walked chamfer
  over a narrow face (the check for that took the pieces' lines,
  parametrized as the spine, for walked ones).

Nothing else changes: roundings, chamfers whose ends are made otherwise,
and chamfers that add material keep their ends as before.

Upstream: new.
